      </constraints>
      <costs>
        <cost name="pts" typeId="e7de-8dcf-403a-b76a" value="0"/>
      </costs>
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink name="Crusader" id="ae57-0f3e-3ee1-22c0" hidden="false" targetId="9e9f-d95e-6c06-ff3b" type="rule"/>
        <infoLink name="Adamantium Will" id="d1d0-7d8e-a159-d916" hidden="false" targetId="e665-d068-6f9e-bf71" type="rule"/>
        <infoLink name="Counter-Attack" id="b544-6cd5-0a5f-e500" hidden="false" targetId="2a25-a0c2-2424-ea88" type="rule"/>
        <infoLink name="Rage" id="c06a-d56a-51f2-50f5" hidden="false" targetId="8c0c-8856-f1ab-923d" type="rule"/>
      </infoLinks>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Black Templars" id="f5a8-0ca4-d842-5eeb" hidden="false">
          <description>Black Templars models have the Crusader and Adamantium Will (5+) special rules.
If a Black Templars unit suffers one or more casualties in the Shooting phase or as a result of Overwatch or Return Fire, all models in that unit gain the Counter-attack (1) and Rage (2) special rules until the end of the turn.

No model with psychic powers may be fielded by or as an ally of the Black Templars with the exception of the Grey Knights.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Bolter Discipline" id="b299-31b7-42a6-41ee" hidden="false">
          <description>Instead of following the normal rules for Rapid Fire weapons, models in this unit shooting Rapid Fire bolt weapons make double the number of attacks if any of the following apply:
The shooting model’s target is within half the weapon’s range.
The shooting model is INFANTRY and its unit Remained Stationary in your previous Movement phase.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule name="Righteous Zeal" id="b606-6941-81bf-3da3" hidden="false">
          <description>Black Templars automatically pass Fear and Regroup tests. When regrouping, Black Templars units do not make a 3&quot; Regroup move, but can instead move, shoot, run or declare charges normally in that turn. Further, Black Templars units caught by a Sweeping Advance are not destroyed, they instead remain locked in combat.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </selectionEntry>
